PROPOSAL ONLY - NOT APPLIED. Decision input for plan 06-08 Task 3.

This file is a unified diff against .github/workflows/ci.yml as of the commit
recorded below. No task in plan 06-08 edits ci.yml; CLAUDE.md makes modifying a
CI workflow a check-in-before-acting item. Plan 06-09 applies exactly the hunks
the human approves, and nothing if the answer is `defer`.

  git apply --check .planning/phases/06-native-time-series-forecasting-stack/06-ci-chronos-step.patch

HUNK (a) - a new `Chronos embedded-weights gate` step, placed immediately after
the `cargo nextest run --profile ci --workspace --lib` leg. Runs
`just chronos-gate` in the same docker invocation pattern the neighbouring legs
use. D-18 clause 2 ("at least one CI leg actually exercises the embedded-weights
build") is met by this hunk and by nothing else in the file.

HUNK (b) - `cargo test -p aprender-mcp-forecast --test e2e_stdio` appended to
the single physical Integration-tests line, immediately before the trailing
`cargo build --examples --workspace --keep-going`. ci.yml's own comment at that
step says a `tests/*.rs` file "does nothing until its name appears HERE, and
only one PR at a time may edit this single physical line without hitting a
merge-queue conflict" - so this hunk is the merge-conflict-prone half and can be
taken independently of hunk (a).

WHAT THE EXECUTOR CANNOT DO FOR YOU. Hunk (a) needs two things provisioned on
the runner that a workflow edit cannot create:
  1. a weights mount. `/srv/models` in the diff is a PLACEHOLDER; name the real
     path in your reply and 06-09 substitutes it.
  2. a way for `uv run --with huggingface_hub --with safetensors --with numpy`
     to resolve without network inside `sovereign-ci:stable` - a warm uv cache
     mount (the diff proposes `/srv/uv-cache`) or those packages baked into the
     image.
Neither was verified by the executor; both are stated so the decision is made
with them visible rather than discovered in a red CI run.

THE NUMERICAL RISK (REVIEW-06-02). Every CI job is
`[self-hosted, X64, Linux, clean-room]` (ci.yml:96,516,988,1039). The f32
quantile bar `quantiles_abs_f32 = 1.0e-6` was frozen on 9.54e-7 measured on
aarch64 WITH the spike-008 NEON microkernel, ~4.6 % of headroom; on x86_64
`gemm_blis` does not dispatch that microkernel, so accumulation order through a
12-layer T5 differs and the divergence has never been measured. 06-05 added the
PROVISIONAL `quantiles_abs_f32_nonaarch64 = 5.0e-6` which the parity tests
select on `!cfg!(target_arch = "aarch64")`, and every parity test prints the bar
and arch it used - so the first x86_64 run yields the measurement that bar is
waiting for. A red leg is unlikely but possible, and the number it would print
is the number the phase wants.

